                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='56778' id='5' type-v2='text' w='98482' x='759' y='7414'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>Purpose:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>Understand better the customers that are taking part of the subscription program from MENA, PSP Checkout.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>KPI Calculations:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>* Retention Rate (Cohort) -&gt;# of subscribers that have paid for their subscription in the subsequent months after their initial subscription date.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>* Subscription Success Rate (SR) per User -&gt;# of users of successful transactions / # of all users.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>* Subscription Success Rate (SR) per Transaction (Trx) -&gt;# of successful transactions / # of all transactions.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>* Canceled vs. Lost -&gt; If a subscriber&apos;s last transaction (no more existing transactions in subsequent months) in our system has been approved, then we consider that they have canceled their subscription. On the other hand, if a subscriber&apos;s last transaction in our system has not been approved, then we consider that we lost them, since we couldn&apos;t charge them due an online payment issue.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>Time Frame:</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>Æ </run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>Last 12 months</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>Notes:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>* Subscribers are identified based on the field &apos;payment_type&apos;, if a customer has a transaction in this field that equals to &apos;recurring&apos;, then they&apos;ve paid or attempted to pay for a subscription program, and therefore they are understood as subscribers. Transactions where the field &apos;payment_type&apos; equals to &apos;regular&apos; represents the orders the customers have placed.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontname='Segoe UI' fontsize='10'>* An unique subscriber is currently being identified based on a conjunction of two fields: &quot;Business Name (entity)&quot; and &quot;Customer E-mail&quot;. However, ideally they should be identified based on three fields: &quot;Business Name (entity)&quot;, &quot;Customer E-mail&quot; and &quot;Subscription Date (udf4)&quot;. It&apos;s important to have the &quot;Business Name (entity)&quot; together with the &quot;Customer E-mail&quot; because the same e-mail could be registered to different entities (Carriage and Talabat, for example), and if that&apos;s the case, we want to identify them as different customers/subscribers.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='268' h='34618' id='14' is-fixed='true' name='missing_udf4' w='98482' x='759' y='64192'>
